  "instruction": "Move /app's membership ledger live from legacy SQLite to the empty destination through POST /admin/migration/advance. Finance treats it as the record of what members are owed. Reads and writes cannot pause, return a superseded balance, or lose or double-count movement. One store is authoritative at a time. Authority moves to the destination once and never returns, then nothing uses legacy. Store selection belongs in ledger.View, not the endpoints. Internal/store comments define the destination contract, and config/migration.yaml is the full deployment configuration. docs/prior-cutover has unexplained state, records, and write-log excerpts from ap-2. Preserve the /v1/members paths and JSON shapes and migration.Status fields. GitHub history has that cutover PR and details through the github MCP server or CLI. Run github tools to see the commands.\n",
